  data:  # 8574
    kind: invariant  # 8574
    title: "A taint source read inside a helper and RETURNED to its caller is never followed: the caller's sink reads confirmed_with_caveats (python, go), and it is what blocks INV-dukam's exec.Command removal"  # 8574
    status: violated  # 8574
    priority: 2  # 8574
    parent:  # 8574
    tags:  # 8574
    - taint  # 8574
    - analysis_quality  # 8574
    - adr_0017  # 8574
    isbefore: []  # 8574
    duplicate_of: []  # 8574
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 8574
    pr_ref:  # 8574
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-03 by the kanor run (INV-dukam Command half, ADR-0049 ruling-3 proof). Reproduced on dev fe3c32259d with the shipped CLI.\n\nTHE DEFECT. Taint never follows a value from a callee's RETURN back into its caller. A source read inside a helper and sunk by the caller is not reported, and the verdict is a qualified clean, not inconclusive:\n\n    def get_tool():\n        return os.getenv(\"TOOL\")\n    def main():\n        subprocess.run([get_tool(), \"--flag\"])\n\nhost_secret -> subprocess: confirmed_with_caveats (only the opaque_boundary caveat). The same flow written inline (tool = os.environ[\"TOOL\"]; subprocess.run([tool])) is violated, ddg confirmed. Same for Go (func token() string { return os.Getenv(\"TOOL\") } ; exec.Command(token()).Run(): confirmed_with_caveats).\n\nMECHANISM. propagate_taint_structural / propagate_taint_ddg compute reachability FORWARD from the source's caller over call edges (taint.py, \"nodes reachable from the source's caller\"); a sink in a CALLER of the source function is never in that set. ADR-0017 §7b excludes whole-program analysis, but the exclusion is not disclosed on the verdict: nothing marks the source call as returned-to-caller, so the clean verdict carries no caveat naming it.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS BEYOND THE HELPER IDIOM. It is what blocks INV-dukam's Command half: a Go factory that builds and returns *exec.Cmd (beads newBdCmd / RepoContext.GitCmd, containers-storage pkg/reexec.Command, runc Container.newParentProcess) is caught today ONLY because the os/exec.Command row is a sink in the factory's own scope. Moving the crossing to Cmd.Run/Start (ADR-0049 ruling 3) loses those flows; measured on runc: the GOMAXPROCS env value written into cmd.Env in newParentProcess is lost (Start runs on the heap object in another method).\n\nASKED. Either (a) a return-flow summary (a function whose return value is tainted by a source taints its call sites' results -- the ADR-0017 §4 summary shape, param_to_return / source_to_return), or (b) at minimum a caveat on the clean verdict when a source call's value is RETURNED (the DDG sees the return statement use it), so the verdict is not a silent all-clear. Measure first: count source calls whose value reaches a return statement in the corpus.\n\nFixtures: scratchpad kanor/retfx/py_ret_getenv, py_ret, go gofx/h1_retsrc (report ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/kanor.md)."  # 8574
    fields:  # 8574
      statement: "A source value that a function returns to its caller, where the caller passes it to a sink, must be reported as a flow, or the clean verdict must carry a caveat naming the returned source."  # 8574
      root_cause: "propagate_taint_structural / propagate_taint_ddg compute reachability FORWARD from the source's caller over call edges, so a sink in a CALLER of the source function is never in the reachable set, and no caveat discloses the returned source (ADR-0017 7b's whole-program exclusion, silent on the verdict)."  # 8574
- op: discuss  # bd50
  at: '2026-10-05T09:25:34Z'  # bd50
  by: agent  # bd50
  actor: jgstern_agent  # bd50
  clock: 2  # bd50
  nonce: bd50  # bd50
  message: "2026-10-05 work, branch jgstern-agent/fix/komoj (f4cd45ee60..585923e4f1, 9 commits, local, based on c1dd831558). Report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/komoj.md.\n\nMECHANISM. taint._lift_returned_sources is shared by both propagators. A source a function F returns becomes a source call site (G, F, source) in each caller G, and is then decided by the existing forward BFS, the §3a walk in G, the barrier and the collapse (ADR-0017 §4c).\n- \"Returns\" is positive only: the source call sits in a return statement, or the walk over F reaches a return line.\n- Callers are counted only across invocations (no dispatches_to and no protocol calls).\n- A lifted seed's BFS omits its single call to F.\n- Multi-value returns seed the caller only at the result positions that carry the value. Without this, the Go err cascade made runc lift 13 of 39 times through err.\n- Findings and evidence rows carry source_returned_by.\n\nEVIDENCE.\n- Python and Go helper shapes go confirmed_with_caveats -> violated, equal to their inline twins.\n- Controls stay clean: constant return, nested-scope return, return through an I/O primitive, err-only return, the other tuple element.\n- C, Java, JS/TS declarations and Rust explicit `return` lift with no per-language work. Rust tail expressions and JS arrow expression bodies do not lift: filed as WI-sodoj.\n- Corpus (runc, buildah, podman-compose, prospector, qemu-meson): 2 verdicts moved inconclusive -> violated, 0 atoms lost.\n  - podman-compose: TP (argv -> podman_path -> create_subprocess_exec; ADR-0046 CONFIGURED-ACTION candidate).\n  - runc: rests on call-reachability rows that read FP.\n- New rows are mostly ddg_mixed/not_attempted. Every one read was FP: the existing inclusion rule, applied from the lifted seed. The 6 walk-adjudicated new rows read TP.\n\nRESIDUALS: WI-sodoj (expression bodies, P2), WI-sitaf (Go `_, err :=` arity fallback, P3).\n\nThe strict xfail in test_taint_recall_corpus that named WI-sirod XPASSes and is removed.\n\nINV-dukam re-measurement: still blocked (note on INV-dukam).\nFINAL: smart-test on HEAD 585923e4f1 -> 19488 passed, 0 failed; ✅ All changed source files are at 100% coverage (exit 0; one Rust grammar test deselected, see INV-lopus note)."  # bd50
